    "title": "Emergency bridge repairs to close 3 lanes of northbound I-95 in Howard County - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Siobhan Garrett ,\n18 hours ago\nDrivers traveling on I-95 through Howard County could face delays this weekend as crews make emergency repairs to a bridge near MD 32.\nThe Maryland State Highway Administration says three lanes of northbound I-95 will close before westbound MD 32, Exit 38B, beginning at 9 p.m. Friday, Oct. 30.\nOnly one northbound lane will remain open while crews replace a bridge joint.\nThe work will continue overnight and throughout Saturday, Oct. 31, until the repairs are complete.\nDrivers are being encouraged to plan for delays and consider alternate routes, including US 1, US 29 and MD 295.\nSHA is also reminding drivers approaching the work zone to stay alert, avoid distractions and slow down or move over when necessary.\nThis is a developing story, so check back with WMAR2News.com for updates. Email the WMAR-2 Newsroom if you have info, photos or videos to share.\n📱 More News from WMAR2News.com\nThis story was initially reported by a journalist and has been converted to this platform with the assistance of AI. Our editorial team verifies all reporting on all platforms for fairness and accuracy.",
    "summary": "Drivers traveling on I-95 through Howard County could face delays this weekend as crews make emergency repairs to a bridge near MD 32. The Maryland State Highway Administration says three lanes of northbound I-95 will close before westbound MD 32, Exit 38B, beginning at 9 p.m. Friday, Oct. 30. Drivers are being encouraged to plan for delays and consider alternate routes, including US 1, US 29 and MD 295. SHA is also reminding drivers approaching the work zone to stay alert, avoid distractions and slow down or move over when necessary.",
